  "interpretation": "The requested EGO socket receive buffer took effect: the run-local profile requested 212992 bytes, and ss observed rb=425984 on the callback-thread socket throughout all 49 selected-gap samples. A same-image, same-host profile-free socket smoke observed rb=212992. Increasing the effective buffer did not remove the 2.608 s take gap, and the socket drop counter still rose by 196 during the gap (202 across the bracket). In this run, the reader reported no sample_lost/rejected callback or cumulative status increment. Socket-level drops do not identify ROS topic or RTPS sample and do not establish causality. This single run weakens the hypothesis that buffer size alone explains the gap; it does not locate the packet loss or reader-delivery boundary.",
